<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harima Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harima Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the Inland Sea, now the south-western part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyogo-prefecture">Hyōgo Prefecture</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> it was given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikeda-terumasa">Ikeda Terumasa</a>, who rebuilt Himeji Castle, the province's main stronghold. Later it was divided among several domains, the largest of them Himeji.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harima-province.jpg" alt="Harima Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Harima.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
